Every Sliver you cast cascades — and a cascade cast is still a CAST, so if the free spell is also a Sliver, it cascades too. One five-drop Sliver chains down through the whole curve, and each link is another body, another anthem, and another enters-the-battlefield trigger shared by the entire board. The deck is not really a tribal aggro deck. It is a combo deck whose combo is "cast a Sliver".

# The commander and the chain
The First Sliver :: five colours, a 7/7, and every Sliver spell you cast has cascade. Once he is out, the correct play is almost always "cast the most expensive Sliver in hand" — the chain does the rest.
Morophon, the Boundless :: name Sliver and every Sliver spell costs {W}{U}{B}{R}{G} less. Most of the deck becomes free, and each free cast still cascades.
Maelstrom Nexus :: the first spell you cast each turn cascades, Sliver or not.
Quandrix, the Proof :: your instants and sorceries from hand cascade too.
Maelstrom Wanderer :: two more cascades, and permanent haste for the whole board — which matters because the chain deploys creatures mid-turn.
Apex Devastator :: four cascades on one card.
Call Forth the Tempest :: two cascades plus a sweeper sized by everything the chain has already cast.
Averna, the Chaos Bloom :: every cascade also puts a land onto the battlefield, so a long chain ramps you at the same time.

# Getting paid for the free casts
Nalfeshnee :: every spell cast from exile is COPIED. A cascade chain with Nalfeshnee out doubles every Sliver in it.
Quintorius Kand :: two damage to each opponent and two life to you for EVERY spell cast from exile. A six-link chain is twelve damage to the table before combat.
Lavabelly Sliver :: every Sliver that enters pings a player for one and gains you one. During a chain, that is one trigger per link, on top of everything else.
Harmonic Sliver :: every Sliver that enters destroys an artifact or enchantment. A cascade chain becomes a one-sided Vandalblast on the table's whole board.
Guardian Project :: a card for every differently named nontoken creature — and every Sliver in the deck has a different name.
Kindred Discovery :: name Sliver. A card for every Sliver that enters AND every one that attacks.

# The mana that makes it possible
Gemhide Sliver :: all Slivers tap for any colour. Two Slivers later this is a five-colour mana engine.
Manaweft Sliver :: the second copy.
Basal Sliver :: every Sliver can sacrifice for {B}{B}, which is how you convert a huge board into a huge spell.
Birds of Paradise :: turn-one fixing.
Bloom Tender :: scales with your colours.
Delighted Halfling :: uncounterable mana for legendary spells — The First Sliver himself.
Nature's Lore :: an untapped dual.
Farseek :: a shockland.
Fellwar Stone :: usually taps for exactly what you are missing.
Lotus Bloom :: suspend it on turn one and it is three mana of any colour on turn four.

# The suspend package
Suspended cards are cast for free from EXILE when their last counter is removed, which triggers Nalfeshnee and Quintorius Kand just like a cascade does.
Ancestral Vision :: three cards for one mana, four turns later.
Inevitable Betrayal :: the best creature out of an opponent's library, onto your battlefield.
Profane Tutor :: any card in the deck for two mana on a delay.
Lotus Bloom :: acceleration with no card cost.

# Anthems and evasion
Predatory Sliver :: +1/+1 to the whole team.
Cloudshredder Sliver :: flying AND haste for every Sliver. It is what turns a cascade chain into a lethal attack the same turn.
Galerider Sliver :: the one-mana flying anthem.
Bonescythe Sliver :: double strike for the whole board.
Leeching Sliver :: a life off the defending player for every Sliver that attacks.
Akroma's Will :: with your commander out, take both halves. On a wide Sliver board it simply ends the game.

# Protection and removal
Crystalline Sliver :: all Slivers have shroud. Nothing they play can target your board — but note it stops your own targeting too.
Diffusion Sliver :: the gentler version, taxing their removal two.
Hibernation Sliver :: every Sliver can bounce itself for two life, saving it from removal or resetting an enters trigger.
Quick Sliver :: Slivers gain flash, so you can build the board at the end of their turn.
Necrotic Sliver :: every Sliver can sacrifice to destroy any permanent. On a wide board that is unlimited removal.
Heroic Intervention :: hexproof and indestructible through a wrath.
Assassin's Trophy :: two mana for any permanent.
Cyclonic Rift :: overloaded, the clear for a lethal attack.
Raise the Palisade :: name Sliver and every other creature at the table goes back to hand. A one-sided bounce wrath.
Patriarch's Bidding :: name Sliver. You rebuild your entire graveyard; most tables get far less back.
Homing Sliver :: gives every Sliver in hand slivercycling, so dead cards become the exact Sliver you need.
Mystic Remora :: the best card in the deck on turns one through four.

# What to keep in an opening hand
Keep fixing and a cheap Sliver. Gemhide Sliver or Manaweft Sliver on turn two solves the five-colour problem by itself, because every Sliver you play afterwards is also a mana source.
The First Sliver costs five specific colours. Prioritise Morophon, the mana Slivers and Bloom Tender over another anthem — the deck does nothing until he resolves, and everything once he does.
Cast the most expensive Sliver first. Cascade finds a cheaper card, so leading with a five-drop chains through four-, three-, two- and one-drops; leading with a one-drop finds nothing.
Cloudshredder Sliver :: keep it in mind before you start the chain. Flying and haste means the board you just built attacks this turn, which is usually the difference between a big turn and a lethal one.
